From 383d42e87159dedccc024fa1bfd2813c606a88b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 08:28:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/39] G4 cont4 checkpoint 1.3: the left pass

- The left pass as one contract from the local facts the return home leaves: a seek to the
  left layout's outermost cell, one zoned step across the separator, and two left moves by the
  scratch ruler with the inner- and outer-half writes after them (the displacement's second
  option: two adjusted walks by the half-capacity and the one-cell step).
- The left move: skip the ruler on scratch, two scratch steps back onto its last cell, the
  leftward adjusted walk, two scratch steps back to its first cell; the scratch steps are one
  contract parametrized by direction.
- The ruler step and the adjusted walk parametrized by direction; a generic re-indexing
  adapter; per-stage field lemmas (time, endpoint, envelopes) for the two-step, the walk, the
  move, the writer and the pass.
- The left pass's tape bridge (the extended zoned tape on the nonpositive half-line), the seam
  from the return home, and the level-one instance (outer end at cell -8).
- The seek-to-start premise restated by local facts; the old two-walk arithmetic replaced by the
  displacement actually used.
- Region (c): the extension row's status paragraph updated.

